## Creating users & passwords
Public sign-up is closed: `emailAndPassword.disableSignUp` is set in `packages/auth/src/auth.ts`, so the `/api/auth/sign-up/email` endpoint rejects every call. Admins create users from the Users panel. The form never asks for a password: `user.create` (`packages/api/src/router/user.ts`, `adminProcedure`) generates one server-side with `generatePassword()` (`@repo/auth/password`), creates the account with the default role, gives it the chosen role with `setRole` and returns the password once so the admin can share it. The seed (`scripts/seed.ts`) gives the three demo accounts their role with a write of its own after it created them, as the guard of the `admin` plugin endpoints takes `admin` or the default role at creation. A password can be regenerated anytime from the user detail page (`user.generatePassword`), shown a single time with a copy button.

